 "answer": "To configure LlamaIndex to use a local Ollama LLM and a Hugging Face embedding model, ensuring that OpenAI is never contacted, you can follow these steps. This setup will allow you to run LlamaIndex fully locally, leveraging local resources instead of external APIs.\n\n1. **Install Required Libraries**:\n   Ensure you have the necessary libraries installed. You can install LlamaIndex and any specific embedding libraries via pip:\n\n   ```bash\n   pip install llama-index\n   pip install llama-index-embeddings-openai  # if you want to use OpenAI's embeddings as a reference\n   ```\n\n2. **Configure LlamaIndex with Local Models**:\n   Use the `Settings` object to configure your local LLM and embedding models globally. This configuration will replace the old `ServiceContext` and ensure that the specified models are used throughout LlamaIndex.\n\n   Here’s how you can set it up:\n\n   ```python\n   from llama_index.llms.ollama import Ollama\n   from llama_index.embeddings.huggingface import HuggingFaceEmbedding\n   from llama_index.core import Settings\n\n   # Set Ollama as the local LLM\n   Settings.llm = Ollama()\n\n   # Set Hugging Face Embedding as the global embedding model\n   Settings.embed_model = HuggingFaceEmbedding(model_name=\"sentence-transformers/bert-base-nli-mean-tokens\")\n\n   # Example of using the settings in a VectorStoreIndex\n   from llama_index.core import VectorStoreIndex, SimpleDirectoryReader\n\n   # Read documents\n   documents = SimpleDirectoryReader('path_to_your_documents').load_data()\n\n   # Create an index\n   index = VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(documents)\n   ```\n\n3. **Ensure Local Execution**:\n   By setting the `Settings` object as shown above, you ensure that all components of LlamaIndex use the specified local models. This setup avoids any external API calls, such as those to OpenAI.\n\n4. **Verify Configuration**:\n   To verify that your configuration is correct and that no external API calls are being made, you can run a simple query and check the execution flow:\n\n   ```python\n   query_engine = index.as_query_engine()\n\n   # Run a query\n   response = query_engine.query(\"What is the capital of France?\")\n   print(response)\n   ```\n\n   Ensure that the response is generated using the local models without any external API interactions.\n\nBy following these steps, you can successfully configure LlamaIndex to use a local Ollama LLM and a Hugging Face embedding model, ensuring that OpenAI or any other external service is not contacted.",
